WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.690
- What is the value of completing an MBA?

00:00:02.690 --> 00:00:06.760
since I graduated from
the INSEAD MBA in 2016,

00:00:06.760 --> 00:00:10.110
I got asked this question a
lot from family and friends

00:00:10.110 --> 00:00:12.853
on my Instagram channel Firm
Learning and the last day

00:00:12.853 --> 00:00:16.010
I also posted several pieces
on my learning journey,

00:00:16.010 --> 00:00:18.680
my reflection on what I
took away from the MBA

00:00:18.680 --> 00:00:21.210
and there was well I
received lots of questions on

00:00:21.210 --> 00:00:22.710
whether it's actually worth it

00:00:22.710 --> 00:00:25.050
to complete an MBA in these times.

00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:27.857
In this video, I'm covering
the top five reasons

00:00:27.857 --> 00:00:30.720
why I believe an MBA
might make sense for you.

00:00:30.720 --> 00:00:33.830
So I hope this helps you
to evaluate for yourself

00:00:33.830 --> 00:00:36.680
whether doing an MBA
might be worth your time

00:00:36.680 --> 00:00:37.513
and your money.

00:00:37.513 --> 00:00:38.740
Hi there my name is Heinrich

00:00:38.740 --> 00:00:41.610
and welcome to another coffee
break with Firm Learning.

00:00:41.610 --> 00:00:43.230
If you are already a subscriber,

00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:45.230
I'm so grateful that
you're following me here

00:00:45.230 --> 00:00:48.100
on this YouTube journey and if
you're not a subscriber yet,

00:00:48.100 --> 00:00:50.840
if you take any value out of
this video, please consider

00:00:50.840 --> 00:00:52.980
subscribing and also
hitting the like button

00:00:52.980 --> 00:00:56.180
for the YouTube algorithm.
So what is an MBA program?

00:00:56.180 --> 00:00:59.020
So for those of you who don't
know, just let me give you

00:00:59.020 --> 00:01:01.000
my brief personal definition of it.

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:04.250
The MBA stands for Master
in Business Administration.

00:01:04.250 --> 00:01:05.880
It is an academic degree.

00:01:05.880 --> 00:01:08.270
But the big difference
compared to many other master

00:01:08.270 --> 00:01:11.350
programs that exist in
business, especially in Europe

00:01:11.350 --> 00:01:14.230
is that it is a post experience program.

00:01:14.230 --> 00:01:16.660
This means that you're usually only able

00:01:16.660 --> 00:01:19.510
to get into the program
if you have several years

00:01:19.510 --> 00:01:20.670
of work experience.

00:01:20.670 --> 00:01:23.420
So typical MBA program
would have an average

00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:26.190
work experience of their
class of four years.

00:01:26.190 --> 00:01:28.900
So the average person who
attends an MBA will have four

00:01:28.900 --> 00:01:32.060
years of work experience
and usually the bare minimum

00:01:32.060 --> 00:01:35.290
that you need to have is two
years of work experience.

00:01:35.290 --> 00:01:37.560
And this is often also
only possible if you come

00:01:37.560 --> 00:01:40.126
from a so called accelerated
career environment,

00:01:40.126 --> 00:01:43.500
which is to pretty considered
either consulting or banking.

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:45.430
Where you're assumed
to just have collected

00:01:45.430 --> 00:01:47.960
lots of experience in two
years so most of the time,

00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:50.450
if you come from a more
regular industry background,

00:01:50.450 --> 00:01:53.030
you will be expected to have
at least the full four years

00:01:53.030 --> 00:01:55.500
of experience before you
can enter the program

00:01:55.500 --> 00:01:57.770
and the second key difference
to the more traditional

00:01:57.770 --> 00:02:00.030
business oriented master programs.

00:02:00.030 --> 00:02:01.560
As they exist, especially in Europe,

00:02:01.560 --> 00:02:04.630
is that why these master
programs are usually more focused

00:02:04.630 --> 00:02:07.140
on preparing you for an academic career.

00:02:07.140 --> 00:02:09.140
The MBA is more professional degree

00:02:09.140 --> 00:02:11.170
that is supposed to help you prepare

00:02:11.170 --> 00:02:13.940
to become a manager in the
real world if you wanna

00:02:13.940 --> 00:02:16.300
to put it this way, right?
So really to prepare you

00:02:16.300 --> 00:02:19.050
to succeed in a business environment,

00:02:19.050 --> 00:02:21.100
and not in a specialist role,

00:02:21.100 --> 00:02:23.440
but more in a general management role.

00:02:23.440 --> 00:02:26.010
And so before I talk about
the reasons why I believe it

00:02:26.010 --> 00:02:29.140
could make sense for you to do
an MBA, let me cover the top

00:02:29.140 --> 00:02:31.810
two reasons why you maybe
should not do an MBA.

00:02:31.810 --> 00:02:34.040
And these two reasons come
down to the investment

00:02:34.040 --> 00:02:35.840
that you need to make when doing an MBA.

00:02:35.840 --> 00:02:39.920
And this investment consists
of both time and money.

00:02:39.920 --> 00:02:42.670
So if we look at it at the
time aspect of things and MBA

00:02:42.670 --> 00:02:46.160
program usually takes
either one or two years,

00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:48.050
with some programs in the middle

00:02:48.050 --> 00:02:50.760
and what you would typically
see as the US programs

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:52.720
are on the longer side of the spectrum,

00:02:52.720 --> 00:02:55.230
so rather on the two years side of things,

00:02:55.230 --> 00:02:57.970
whereas the European or
International programs are more

00:02:57.970 --> 00:02:59.960
on the one year side of things.

00:02:59.960 --> 00:03:01.860
Though of course, there
are some deviations

00:03:01.860 --> 00:03:03.470
from that rule in both directions.

00:03:03.470 --> 00:03:06.820
And of course, you need to
realize that one to two years

00:03:06.820 --> 00:03:09.010
are a significant time investment.

00:03:09.010 --> 00:03:11.790
Instead of doing the MBA,
you could work on your career

00:03:11.790 --> 00:03:13.740
in the job that you're currently having,

00:03:13.740 --> 00:03:15.670
and also advance in this job

00:03:15.670 --> 00:03:17.280
in this one to two years of time.

00:03:17.280 --> 00:03:18.450
And you need to be convinced

00:03:18.450 --> 00:03:21.540
that by doing an MBA, you
can actually accelerate

00:03:21.540 --> 00:03:24.920
your career so much that this
loss of time will actually

00:03:24.920 --> 00:03:26.460
be recovered later down the path.

00:03:26.460 --> 00:03:28.600
And the second element of the cost.

00:03:28.600 --> 00:03:31.970
If you currently look into how
expensive an INSEAD MBA is,

00:03:31.970 --> 00:03:33.820
this is the program that I competed.

00:03:33.820 --> 00:03:37.270
It currently costs about 85,000 euro

00:03:37.270 --> 00:03:39.780
for the one year MBA experience.

00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:41.940
So I was lucky that when I completed it,

00:03:41.940 --> 00:03:44.700
I believe it only was 65,000 euros.

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:46.160
So you can see that the cost of these

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:48.480
programs rather tend to go up over time

00:03:48.480 --> 00:03:51.170
and I also had the privilege
to get some funding from

00:03:51.170 --> 00:03:53.685
my employer at that time,
but many other didn't needed

00:03:53.685 --> 00:03:55.270
to pay the full amount.

00:03:55.270 --> 00:03:57.650
When you pay for such a
program you need to consider

00:03:57.650 --> 00:03:59.510
that not only you lose the money,

00:03:59.510 --> 00:04:02.620
but you will in this time
period of the MBA in these

00:04:02.620 --> 00:04:05.130
one or two years, you also cannot work.

00:04:05.130 --> 00:04:06.880
So you're losing the salary,

00:04:06.880 --> 00:04:09.170
the income for this time period as well.

00:04:09.170 --> 00:04:11.610
So it's kind of a double
cost because you need to

00:04:11.610 --> 00:04:15.360
pay for it on one side, and
then also lose the salary of it

00:04:15.360 --> 00:04:18.990
on the other side. So doing
an MBA can be quite expensive.

00:04:18.990 --> 00:04:21.510
And again, you need to
believe that then later down

00:04:21.510 --> 00:04:25.100
the road, you recover the cost
due to an accelerated career

00:04:25.100 --> 00:04:27.640
development and a higher
salary that you incur,

00:04:27.640 --> 00:04:29.620
which you wouldn't have got
if you wouldn't have done

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:30.453
the MBA.

00:04:30.453 --> 00:04:32.640
So is there any basis to
believe that you actually

00:04:32.640 --> 00:04:35.670
can recover this investment?
Well, there are many rankings

00:04:35.670 --> 00:04:39.070
of MBA programs out there. One
of the probably most renowned

00:04:39.070 --> 00:04:41.320
is the Financial Times MBA ranking.

00:04:41.320 --> 00:04:43.250
And in the current 2020 edition,

00:04:43.250 --> 00:04:45.250
you see Harvard Business School on one,

00:04:45.250 --> 00:04:47.350
Wharton of the University of Pennsylvania

00:04:47.350 --> 00:04:50.660
on number two, the Graduate
School of Business from Stanford

00:04:50.660 --> 00:04:53.450
on three and the INSEAD program
on number four in the

00:04:53.450 --> 00:04:54.283
global ranking.

00:04:54.283 --> 00:04:56.250
And in these rankings,
you typically see how

00:04:56.250 --> 00:04:58.990
salaries and other KPIs of the alumni

00:04:58.990 --> 00:05:00.740
of these programs developed.

00:05:00.740 --> 00:05:02.400
So if you don't look
into the Harvard figures,

00:05:02.400 --> 00:05:05.813
the program ranked number
one, you see that the average

00:05:05.813 --> 00:05:09.630
salary of the alumni corrected
for purchase power parity.

00:05:09.630 --> 00:05:13.840
So the weighted version lies
around 210,000 US dollars.

00:05:13.840 --> 00:05:17.730
And this is supposed to
correspond to an increase compared

00:05:17.730 --> 00:05:22.730
to the pre MBA salaries of
110%. Just for your information

00:05:23.510 --> 00:05:26.080
in this financial time ranking
this is measured by looking

00:05:26.080 --> 00:05:27.790
into the salaries of the alumni

00:05:27.790 --> 00:05:30.210
three years after completing the program.

00:05:30.210 --> 00:05:32.990
For the INSEAD MBA the
numbers are a bit lower,

00:05:32.990 --> 00:05:37.190
on average alumnus would
yield a salary of 181,000 US

00:05:37.190 --> 00:05:39.570
dollars, three years after graduation,

00:05:39.570 --> 00:05:44.140
which would correspond to a
salary increase of 101% compared

00:05:44.140 --> 00:05:45.820
to their pre MBA salary.

00:05:45.820 --> 00:05:47.630
Of course, now the Harvard MBA

00:05:47.630 --> 00:05:51.220
is two years while the INSEAD
MBA is one year so the return

00:05:51.220 --> 00:05:53.690
on your investment regarding
time is even higher now

00:05:53.690 --> 00:05:54.530
for the INSEAD one.

00:05:54.530 --> 00:05:57.730
So looking at this, yes, there
seem to be some plausibility

00:05:57.730 --> 00:05:59.977
that after doing these kind of programs,

00:05:59.977 --> 00:06:02.220
you salary can be boosted to level high

00:06:02.220 --> 00:06:05.530
enough that it actually
justifies the time and the money

00:06:05.530 --> 00:06:06.830
that you invest upfront.

00:06:06.830 --> 00:06:09.330
But be aware that this is only a spectrum.

00:06:09.330 --> 00:06:11.630
So while it might be
worthwhile for many people,

00:06:11.630 --> 00:06:13.450
there will still be a
certain group of people

00:06:13.450 --> 00:06:16.000
doing this MBA for whom
it didn't really work out

00:06:16.000 --> 00:06:16.833
as they hoped.

00:06:16.833 --> 00:06:19.140
And of course, these are
some of the most renowned

00:06:19.140 --> 00:06:21.610
some of the flagship
MBA programs out there.

00:06:21.610 --> 00:06:24.940
There are many, many other
MBA programs which have KPIs

00:06:24.940 --> 00:06:27.320
that fall short and of
course, you need to be aware

00:06:27.320 --> 00:06:30.200
that these programs are some
of the globally leading ones.

00:06:30.200 --> 00:06:32.810
And it's not guaranteed that
you get admitted to them,

00:06:32.810 --> 00:06:34.800
you need to show a certain
level of professional

00:06:34.800 --> 00:06:37.350
and academic performance
in order to get admitted.

00:06:37.350 --> 00:06:40.170
So you might be stuck with
one of the lower tier programs

00:06:40.170 --> 00:06:43.370
and the stats of these programs
usually are not as good

00:06:43.370 --> 00:06:44.720
but then on the other
hand side of the cost

00:06:44.720 --> 00:06:46.520
also not as high.

00:06:46.520 --> 00:06:49.210
So now we talked about
two more obvious things,

00:06:49.210 --> 00:06:51.700
time and money and why
this is super relevant,

00:06:51.700 --> 00:06:54.560
and probably most people
already think about if they ask

00:06:54.560 --> 00:06:56.660
themselves whether they wanted one MBA.

00:06:56.660 --> 00:06:59.374
In this video, I'd like
to cover five reasons

00:06:59.374 --> 00:07:02.490
five advantages that I
got from doing an MBA,

00:07:02.490 --> 00:07:05.090
which I believe are less
obvious or maybe less clear

00:07:05.090 --> 00:07:07.140
to many of you who think about doing that.

00:07:07.140 --> 00:07:09.090
So I'd like to cover
this in this video now.

00:07:09.090 --> 00:07:12.480
And of course, now I forgot
one of the biggest advantages

00:07:12.480 --> 00:07:15.300
of doing an MBA. And this
is that you're going to get

00:07:15.300 --> 00:07:18.870
all kinds of great and crazy shirts.

00:07:18.870 --> 00:07:22.560
I mean, look at this amazing
sports shirt off the INSEAD MBA

00:07:22.560 --> 00:07:24.510
this is what you would get as well.

00:07:24.510 --> 00:07:25.740
Doesn't matter where you do it.

00:07:25.740 --> 00:07:27.680
But now jokes aside back to the video.

00:07:27.680 --> 00:07:29.730
So let's start with number one.

00:07:29.730 --> 00:07:33.870
And this is looking at the
MBA as some kind of Joker card

00:07:33.870 --> 00:07:34.703
that you have.

00:07:34.703 --> 00:07:37.140
After the first years of your career,

00:07:37.140 --> 00:07:41.240
you might find yourself already
kind of stuck in a certain

00:07:41.240 --> 00:07:44.490
box in the corporate world
maybe you're an accountant

00:07:44.490 --> 00:07:46.110
or you're a controller

00:07:46.110 --> 00:07:48.400
or you did lots of marketing and sales.

00:07:48.400 --> 00:07:50.640
And you're afraid that
if you just continue

00:07:50.640 --> 00:07:52.760
your career, the way
you're currently doing it,

00:07:52.760 --> 00:07:55.260
you will be just so
stuck into this position

00:07:55.260 --> 00:07:57.950
that it will be really
difficult for you at some point

00:07:57.950 --> 00:08:00.410
to transition into a completely new role.

00:08:00.410 --> 00:08:03.810
So one of the reasons
that people do an MBA for

00:08:03.810 --> 00:08:06.670
and I found out by looking
into my peers in the MBA

00:08:06.670 --> 00:08:10.500
that this works really well
is to make a bold transition

00:08:10.500 --> 00:08:11.670
into a new role.

00:08:11.670 --> 00:08:13.620
And if you think about it, conceptually,

00:08:13.620 --> 00:08:16.530
most people think of doing
these kind of conditions

00:08:16.530 --> 00:08:18.950
in three dimensions, you
can either transition

00:08:18.950 --> 00:08:22.290
to a new geography, or you
can transition into a new

00:08:22.290 --> 00:08:25.660
industry, or you can
transition into a new function.

00:08:25.660 --> 00:08:28.900
So regarding geography, maybe
you currently work in Europe,

00:08:28.900 --> 00:08:31.380
and you'd like to make the
transition to work in Asia

00:08:31.380 --> 00:08:32.213
on the US.

00:08:32.213 --> 00:08:34.160
So doing an MBA can help you with that,

00:08:34.160 --> 00:08:36.730
or you would like to change
industry, maybe you've worked

00:08:36.730 --> 00:08:39.450
a lot in automotive, and now
you'd like to work for retail

00:08:39.450 --> 00:08:40.510
or for healthcare.

00:08:40.510 --> 00:08:43.690
Again, doing an MBA can be helpful to you,

00:08:43.690 --> 00:08:45.870
or you'd like to change functions.

00:08:45.870 --> 00:08:47.950
So currently, you worked
a managerial accounting

00:08:47.950 --> 00:08:49.700
or you've worked in production,

00:08:49.700 --> 00:08:51.400
or you worked in marketing and sales,

00:08:51.400 --> 00:08:53.380
and you'd like to switch
to another function.

00:08:53.380 --> 00:08:55.820
So it doesn't matter which
of these three dimensions

00:08:55.820 --> 00:08:57.350
you would like to change.

00:08:57.350 --> 00:08:59.150
The MBA is like a joker card

00:08:59.150 --> 00:09:01.600
that you can pull out once in your career,

00:09:01.600 --> 00:09:04.620
and it can help you to
make this transition.

00:09:04.620 --> 00:09:07.610
Because on the MBA, you
get exposure to all these

00:09:07.610 --> 00:09:10.477
new sectors, all these new
fields, roads, you can take

00:09:10.477 --> 00:09:13.900
new courses that are relevant
to the new role that you'd

00:09:13.900 --> 00:09:14.750
like to take.

00:09:14.750 --> 00:09:17.085
And all of this will help you transition

00:09:17.085 --> 00:09:18.090
into your new field.

00:09:18.090 --> 00:09:19.633
The only thing that many people

00:09:19.633 --> 00:09:23.120
will give you as an advice
is to not try to change

00:09:23.120 --> 00:09:26.320
all these three dimensions
at the same time.

00:09:26.320 --> 00:09:30.170
So do not try to change
the geography, the industry

00:09:30.170 --> 00:09:32.560
and the function at the
same time if you're looking

00:09:32.560 --> 00:09:36.150
to do a transition after the
MBA, but try to keep at least

00:09:36.150 --> 00:09:38.740
one of these three dimensions constant,

00:09:38.740 --> 00:09:41.030
and try to only change two of them.

00:09:41.030 --> 00:09:43.370
Because experience shows that otherwise,

00:09:43.370 --> 00:09:45.210
you will have quite some difficulties

00:09:45.210 --> 00:09:46.860
and the change is just too much.

00:09:46.860 --> 00:09:50.010
But of course, if this is
what you really want to do,

00:09:50.010 --> 00:09:52.630
there's always a way to
make these things happen

00:09:52.630 --> 00:09:54.170
if this is what you're really after.

00:09:54.170 --> 00:09:57.181
So the second reason is
regarding the type of content

00:09:57.181 --> 00:10:00.190
that you learn and what does
this thing to have about MBAs

00:10:00.190 --> 00:10:03.280
is that because they do not
have so much in academic focus,

00:10:03.280 --> 00:10:07.150
they can focus much more on
teaching your practical skills

00:10:07.150 --> 00:10:10.180
that you will not find in typical
other university programs.

00:10:10.180 --> 00:10:13.470
So as I am someone who has
already studied business

00:10:13.470 --> 00:10:15.750
in an undergraduate level,
so the business degree

00:10:15.750 --> 00:10:17.230
from the University of Munich

00:10:17.230 --> 00:10:20.090
and then I even have a
master's degree in finance

00:10:20.090 --> 00:10:21.790
from the London School of Economics.

00:10:21.790 --> 00:10:25.140
So even for people who
already have business exposure

00:10:25.140 --> 00:10:26.560
in the university fields,

00:10:26.560 --> 00:10:29.990
it is true that if you do
an MBA, there will be some

00:10:29.990 --> 00:10:33.120
repetition because the MBA
program does not assume

00:10:33.120 --> 00:10:36.060
that all the people already
have a business background.

00:10:36.060 --> 00:10:39.980
So teaches you foundational
courses, which will be some kind

00:10:39.980 --> 00:10:42.410
of repetition if you already
have a business degree,

00:10:42.410 --> 00:10:44.960
but the truth is then that
later on there will be lots

00:10:44.960 --> 00:10:47.470
and lots of courses,
which you will likely not

00:10:47.470 --> 00:10:51.100
have had in your regular
standard University undergrad

00:10:51.100 --> 00:10:51.933
business degree.

00:10:51.933 --> 00:10:53.570
So to give you some examples at INSEAD

00:10:53.570 --> 00:10:56.050
there were courses
offered or negotiations.

00:10:56.050 --> 00:10:59.380
So how do you negotiate and
we did lots of role plays

00:10:59.380 --> 00:11:01.550
with professional negotiation coaches

00:11:01.550 --> 00:11:03.310
to improve our negotiation skills.

00:11:03.310 --> 00:11:05.600
We had a course on corporate turnarounds

00:11:05.600 --> 00:11:07.790
So how would you actually handle a company

00:11:07.790 --> 00:11:11.330
a situation where the company
is in too heavy financial

00:11:11.330 --> 00:11:13.690
distress, and you will
need to turn around?

00:11:13.690 --> 00:11:16.340
What are the implications
of that? How do you behave

00:11:16.340 --> 00:11:19.450
in this kind of context as
a manager, and of course,

00:11:19.450 --> 00:11:22.640
lots of courses on entrepreneurship
on building businesses

00:11:22.640 --> 00:11:24.580
on identifying new business models,

00:11:24.580 --> 00:11:27.080
and many other aspects of
it. So this is really hands

00:11:27.080 --> 00:11:29.710
on experience that you will
not get in most other more

00:11:29.710 --> 00:11:32.640
academia focused master
or bachelor programs.

00:11:32.640 --> 00:11:35.000
And this is what is so
special about the content

00:11:35.000 --> 00:11:36.270
that is taught at an MBA.

00:11:36.270 --> 00:11:39.330
The third reason for doing
an MBA is the network

00:11:39.330 --> 00:11:40.163
that you build.

00:11:40.163 --> 00:11:42.200
And this is a bit of a cliche point,

00:11:42.200 --> 00:11:44.530
there are people out there
who claim that getting

00:11:44.530 --> 00:11:47.010
and building a network is
one of the main reasons

00:11:47.010 --> 00:11:50.120
to do an MBA so while I
wouldn't necessarily agree

00:11:50.120 --> 00:11:53.280
with that, I agree that it
is one of the key advantages

00:11:53.280 --> 00:11:56.170
of doing it during your
MBA program, you will have

00:11:56.170 --> 00:11:59.270
the opportunity to build
friendships and deep relationships

00:11:59.270 --> 00:12:01.470
with the so many of your classmates

00:12:01.470 --> 00:12:03.503
and there will be
friendships coming out of it

00:12:03.503 --> 00:12:05.220
that really last your whole life.

00:12:05.220 --> 00:12:08.020
And when you choose what
program is right for you,

00:12:08.020 --> 00:12:10.240
I would recommend you
that you also have a look

00:12:10.240 --> 00:12:12.550
what geography your
program is focusing on.

00:12:12.550 --> 00:12:15.420
So if you, for instance, aim
to build a career for yourself

00:12:15.420 --> 00:12:19.080
in the US after your MBA, it
would likely make lots of sense

00:12:19.080 --> 00:12:22.570
to also do an MBA program,
which is in the US,

00:12:22.570 --> 00:12:25.650
because this will help you
to build a deeper network

00:12:25.650 --> 00:12:28.930
in the US if however, you'd
like to rather work in Asia,

00:12:28.930 --> 00:12:31.590
probably doing an MBA
somewhere and that geography

00:12:31.590 --> 00:12:32.977
might make more sense for you.

00:12:32.977 --> 00:12:35.575
But especially the INSEAD
MBA for me is that one of the

00:12:35.575 --> 00:12:38.870
distinguishing factors of
the INSEAD MBA experience

00:12:38.870 --> 00:12:42.490
is that it wants to be an
especially international program,

00:12:42.490 --> 00:12:44.426
so tries to really balance out the class.

00:12:44.426 --> 00:12:47.030
There's no one dominating culture,

00:12:47.030 --> 00:12:50.150
no one dominating geography in the class.

00:12:50.150 --> 00:12:53.010
So we really have contacts
from literally all around the

00:12:53.010 --> 00:12:55.167
world after you complete the program.

00:12:55.167 --> 00:12:58.140
And this for me means now
pretty much doesn't matter

00:12:58.140 --> 00:13:00.170
which country I want to visit

00:13:00.170 --> 00:13:02.900
or which country I might
work in in the future,

00:13:02.900 --> 00:13:05.010
there will be some
people who I can call up

00:13:05.010 --> 00:13:06.280
and talk to them afterwards.

00:13:06.280 --> 00:13:08.340
And this, of course, is
a great feeling not only

00:13:08.340 --> 00:13:09.700
from the professional perspective,

00:13:09.700 --> 00:13:11.830
but also from my private
and personal life.

00:13:11.830 --> 00:13:14.940
The fourth key reason from
my perspective to do an MBA

00:13:14.940 --> 00:13:17.750
is the cultural awareness that you build.

00:13:17.750 --> 00:13:20.610
And again, this depends a bit
on what program you choose

00:13:20.610 --> 00:13:22.960
what the profile of this program is,

00:13:22.960 --> 00:13:25.600
but INSEAD was a highly
international program

00:13:25.600 --> 00:13:28.037
and just meeting all these
people from that many cultures

00:13:28.037 --> 00:13:30.730
really had a big positive
impact on my life.

00:13:30.730 --> 00:13:34.240
During my MBA, I had the
opportunity to spend half the time

00:13:34.240 --> 00:13:35.640
in the French campus,

00:13:35.640 --> 00:13:38.200
but the other half also
in the Singapore campus.

00:13:38.200 --> 00:13:41.300
So spend roughly half a
year in Asia in Singapore,

00:13:41.300 --> 00:13:42.740
and it would be very typical.

00:13:42.740 --> 00:13:45.590
And I heard this a lot from
people doing other MBA programs

00:13:45.590 --> 00:13:48.830
as well so this is not only
specific to the INSEAD program,

00:13:48.830 --> 00:13:52.650
but would be very typical
that almost every weekend,

00:13:52.650 --> 00:13:56.540
there would be all kinds of
trips being organized by people

00:13:56.540 --> 00:13:58.610
who are native of
different other countries

00:13:58.610 --> 00:13:59.960
to then visit this country

00:13:59.960 --> 00:14:01.750
with a bunch of other MBA friends,

00:14:01.750 --> 00:14:06.010
so in the one year of my MBA
program, I was in Israel.

00:14:06.010 --> 00:14:09.560
I was in Singapore, of
course, I was in Vietnam.

00:14:09.560 --> 00:14:12.420
I was in Indonesia. I was in Thailand.

00:14:12.420 --> 00:14:14.880
I spent two weeks with friends in India.

00:14:14.880 --> 00:14:16.947
I was in China, I was in the US.

00:14:16.947 --> 00:14:19.240
And this is just a selection
of all the countries

00:14:19.240 --> 00:14:20.073
that I was in.

00:14:20.073 --> 00:14:22.330
And to be honest, before I did the MBA,

00:14:22.330 --> 00:14:24.080
as somebody who lived in Europe,

00:14:24.080 --> 00:14:27.570
Asia was a pretty faraway place for me.

00:14:27.570 --> 00:14:30.370
I was there a couple
of times for holidays.

00:14:30.370 --> 00:14:34.210
But I really didn't have any
clue what Asia was all about.

00:14:34.210 --> 00:14:37.090
But now after I've spent
half a year of my life

00:14:37.090 --> 00:14:40.630
in Singapore, after I've
visited so many countries there

00:14:40.630 --> 00:14:44.300
and I've met so many local
people during the MBA program,

00:14:44.300 --> 00:14:46.690
this really opened up my
mind and I have a completely

00:14:46.690 --> 00:14:48.300
different relationship with the continent

00:14:48.300 --> 00:14:51.410
and I could very well imagine
to live there to work there

00:14:51.410 --> 00:14:52.620
to spend my time there.

00:14:52.620 --> 00:14:55.090
This really has helped me
a lot to better understand

00:14:55.090 --> 00:14:56.120
this whole continent.

00:14:56.120 --> 00:14:58.720
Though of course, it is clear
that given the diversity

00:14:58.720 --> 00:15:01.030
of cultures and countries
on the continent,

00:15:01.030 --> 00:15:03.750
whatever I have learned
can only be a brief scratch

00:15:03.750 --> 00:15:04.583
of the surface.

00:15:04.583 --> 00:15:07.540
And the last key advantage of
doing an MBA that I like to

00:15:07.540 --> 00:15:10.953
share with you is that it
really is a time where it helps

00:15:10.953 --> 00:15:13.911
you to self reflect on yourself,

00:15:13.911 --> 00:15:16.300
on your goals and on your ambitions.

00:15:16.300 --> 00:15:19.360
So while I was working at
McKinsey before the MBA,

00:15:19.360 --> 00:15:21.830
there was really little time to rest.

00:15:21.830 --> 00:15:23.800
And while I learned an
insane amount of things,

00:15:23.800 --> 00:15:27.170
were working at McKinsey, there
was really little downtime,

00:15:27.170 --> 00:15:30.470
really the time that allowed
me to just introspect,

00:15:30.470 --> 00:15:33.150
to self-reflect, and to ask myself,

00:15:33.150 --> 00:15:35.920
what the right move for
me as now going forward.

00:15:35.920 --> 00:15:39.010
And the MBA really is
a great time for that.

00:15:39.010 --> 00:15:40.200
Because it's not only that,

00:15:40.200 --> 00:15:42.510
you will often have a bit
more time for yourself

00:15:42.510 --> 00:15:44.100
than during your regular work.

00:15:44.100 --> 00:15:47.220
But also given the fact that
you have all these inspirations

00:15:47.220 --> 00:15:50.230
from the courses that you take
from the people that study

00:15:50.230 --> 00:15:52.570
with you from the
countries that you visit.

00:15:52.570 --> 00:15:56.130
All of these inspirations
really help you to take a step

00:15:56.130 --> 00:15:59.340
back and ask yourself what
you really want what your

00:15:59.340 --> 00:16:00.173
objectives are.

00:16:00.173 --> 00:16:02.687
What you want to do in the future in this,

00:16:02.687 --> 00:16:05.332
again helps you to make the
right decisions for you what you

00:16:05.332 --> 00:16:07.060
wanna do after the MBA.

00:16:07.060 --> 00:16:10.590
So guys, I was just out here on the run,

00:16:10.590 --> 00:16:13.430
where I remember even another
reason even another advantage

00:16:13.430 --> 00:16:16.740
of doing an MBA that I forgot
in this is that an MBA,

00:16:16.740 --> 00:16:20.090
which were just the crazy
change of environment.

00:16:20.090 --> 00:16:23.030
It can really help you reset your habits.

00:16:23.030 --> 00:16:25.750
And what I mean by that,
just as an example, you know,

00:16:25.750 --> 00:16:28.290
before the MBA when I
was working at McKinsey,

00:16:28.290 --> 00:16:32.410
I really struggled with
sports, doing sports regularly,

00:16:32.410 --> 00:16:37.410
who really, some really
struggled with sports,

00:16:37.520 --> 00:16:39.140
but because of the change of environment,

00:16:39.140 --> 00:16:41.950
because of all the new impressions
that I had during my MBA,

00:16:41.950 --> 00:16:46.110
this really helped me to pick
up a regular running habit.

00:16:46.110 --> 00:16:48.880
So I literally went
from not running at all

00:16:48.880 --> 00:16:50.290
to running regularly.

00:16:50.290 --> 00:16:53.980
And then shortly after the
MBA, I did a full marathon.

00:16:53.980 --> 00:16:57.520
So 42 kilometers 26 miles,

00:16:57.520 --> 00:17:00.210
which I did sub 4 hours which
was a great success for me.

00:17:00.210 --> 00:17:02.940
And surely this would
have not had happened.

00:17:02.940 --> 00:17:04.220
If I wouldn't have done the MBA.

00:17:04.220 --> 00:17:06.332
And I mean just look at the environment.

00:17:06.332 --> 00:17:07.770
These are just all the side products.

00:17:07.770 --> 00:17:10.410
And this is also one of the
effects for me for sure.

00:17:10.410 --> 00:17:12.810
That came out for me for the MBA.

00:17:12.810 --> 00:17:15.310
So take care all of you
and enjoy have a good day.

00:17:15.310 --> 00:17:18.910
So these are my five reasons
that after reflecting on myself

00:17:18.910 --> 00:17:21.510
is what I think I got out of the MBA most

00:17:21.510 --> 00:17:23.981
to this is not to say
that an MBA makes sense

00:17:23.981 --> 00:17:25.190
for everyone.

00:17:25.190 --> 00:17:27.760
So whether an MBA is
worthwhile for you depends on,

00:17:27.760 --> 00:17:30.300
I think lots of factors
are outlined a few also

00:17:30.300 --> 00:17:32.410
in the beginning regarding
the time investment

00:17:32.410 --> 00:17:33.830
and the money investment.

00:17:33.830 --> 00:17:37.040
But I hope this video helps
you make these deliberations

00:17:37.040 --> 00:17:39.930
for your Senate, and also
hope to have added a few more

00:17:39.930 --> 00:17:43.300
considerations and reasons which
maybe were not that obvious

00:17:43.300 --> 00:17:45.590
for you when you were
thinking about doing an MBA.

